<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1979</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre was a Peruvian political leader who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a> in 1924 as a continental anti-imperialist movement and led it for more than half a century. Repeatedly imprisoned or exiled, and barred by the army from taking power, he spent five years in asylum in the Colombian embassy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>. He presided over the Constituent Assembly that drafted the constitution of 1979 and died that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-raul-haya-de-la-torre.jpg" alt="Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%ADctor_Ra%C3%BAl_Haya_de_la_Torre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
